===persian===

شهر تاریک است
کوچه های خسته در هذیان خواب آلود
می سوزد...
چشم شهر از دود می سوزد.
شهربانان آتشی افروخته
با بوته های جهل
آتشی که گفته اند...
این نور جاوید است....
جاودانه آتش بیدار خورشید است....
.... دروغی را که باید کرد باور
خنجر رنجی ست.
جان از این معنا که
ما با رنج می سازیم... می سوزد
جز دل سنگین دژخیمان
هر چه در آتش می اندازیم میسوزد.
موسم خواری ست...
موسمی که معنی فریاد آشوب است...
غنچه ها می پژ مرد در سردی دلها
و.... گل فریاد بر لبها نمی روید.
موسم خواری ست...
هر که بر لب قفل دارد
دست هایش شاخ پرباری ست.
شهر .... دشت تشنه را ماند
آب میخواهد.
شهربان پیر اما....
شهریان را خواب میخواهد

۱۳۴۷

===machine===

The city is dark
The tired streets in sleepy delirium
Burns...
The eyes of the city burn with smoke.
The city guards have lit a fire
With the bushes of ignorance
The fire that they have said...
This is the eternal light...
The eternal fire is the awakened sun...
.... Believe the lie that must be told
The dagger of suffering.
The soul, in the sense that
We build with suffering... burns
Except for the heavy hearts of our murderers
Whatever we throw into the fire burns.
It is the season of humiliation...
A season that means the cry of chaos...
The buds wither and die in the coldness of hearts
And.... The flower of a cry does not grow on the lips.
It is the season of humiliation...
Whoever has a lock on his lips
His hands are fruitful horns.
The city.... has become a thirsty plain
He wants water.
The old mayor, but....
He wants the citizens to sleep

1347

===lantern===

The city is dark.
Its weary alleys, in a drowsy delirium,
are burning...
the city's eye burns with smoke.
The constables have kindled a fire
out of the brushwood of ignorance —
a fire they have called
the everlasting light...
"the eternal fire is the waking sun"...
The lie one is forced to believe
is a dagger of pain.
The soul burns at this "meaning"
we are made to build out of suffering;
everything we throw on the fire burns —
all but the stony hearts of the hangmen.
It is the season of humiliation...
a season that spells the cry of riot...
Buds shrivel in the cold of hearts,
and no flower-of-protest blooms on the lips.
It is the season of humiliation...
and whoever keeps his lips locked,
his hands are a laden bough.
The city has become a parched plain,
it begs for water —
but the old constable
wants its people asleep.

1347

